title: log panel
tags: Panel [[Event log]]
kind: reference
summary: The repository's history, label by label — badges saying what each is, the watcher's labels hideable, a cursor that reaches single operations.

Open it with `panel:open here log` (<<key "panel:open here log" "t o">>). One row per
label the listed operations are in (their innermost one, [[Labels and contexts]]),
newest first: its number and name, the time of its newest operation, its operation count
and ''status'' badges — what decides whether undoing it makes sense. The nesting of the
labels is not drawn yet: the panel as a tree of labels is the next step of
[[The operation log]].

* `HEAD` — the label of the newest operation;
* `watcher` — the daemon wrote it for the filesystem ([[Operations and their origin]]); the row is dimmed, and `log:undo` skips it;
* `undo of #N` — it is itself a revert of `#N`;
* `undone by #N` — a later revert put it back; its number is struck through, and reverting it again says so first.

An expanded operation that reverted another names it, and one that was reverted is marked
`undone`: a correction and its cause read from each other.

!! Moving around

* <<key "log:next" "↓ or j">> / <<key "log:prev" "↑ or k">>, <<key "log:first" Home>> / <<key "log:last" End>>, <<key "log:find" f>> (a label by number or name, [[Jumping to an entry]]) — the selection, over every listed row.
* <<key "log:toggle ops" Enter>> (or a double click) — expand a label into its operations, and collapse it. The cursor then walks the operations too, and a revert aims at the operation under it.
* <<key "log:toggle watcher" Shift+w>> — hide or show the watcher's labels (shown by default). A display filter over what was fetched: the newest label is never hidden, and the status line says how many are. A selection inside a label that gets hidden is dropped.
* ''Show older operations'' — the list fetches the newest thousand operations, so a repository with millions of them still opens; the button widens the window by as much again.
* <<key "log:refresh" r>> — read the log again. The status line gives how many labels and operations are listed, and the repository's totals when the window is only part of the log.

!! Acting

<<key "log:revert" Shift+r>>, <<key "log:revert op" Shift+o>>, <<key "log:revert label" Shift+v>>,
`log:prune` — and the global <<key "log:undo" Ctrl+z>> / <<key "log:redo" Ctrl+Shift+z>>,
also as toolbar buttons: [[Revision commands in the GUI]].

The cursor is published as `selected_log_entry`, which the [[log-detail panel]] follows.
